# <type>(<scope>): <summary>   ← 50 chars, imperative, no trailing period
#
# <body: what changed and why. Wrap at 72. The why is the point —
#  the diff already shows the what.>
#
# Intent: I-nn        ← required footer. Or: ADR: nnn | Chore: <what>
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conventional Commits — see docs/contributing.md
#
#   type   feat | fix | docs | refactor | test | chore
#   scope  effort | objectives | reviews | parking | time
#          | ci | db | contract | infra
#
# Every commit ends with a footer naming what asked for it:
#
#   Intent: I-nn    work an intent asked for
#   ADR: nnn        platform work whose intent is an ADR
#   Chore: <what>   housekeeping nothing asked for
#
# `Story: W<week>-<nn>` is the historical form and is still accepted, so
# commits made before the move to intents keep validating.
# Enforced by scripts/check-commits.mjs.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
